+### refresh_models
+
+Reload `models.json` without replacing the session. This command does not perform network model discovery. It preserves the current model selection, extension instances, and queued messages. Use `set_model` after a successful refresh to apply a changed descriptor, even when the provider and model ID are unchanged.
+
+```json
+{"type": "refresh_models"}
+```
+
+Response data contains `models` (the available model snapshot), `aborted`, and `errors` (provider IDs mapped to error messages). Treat `aborted: true` or nonempty `errors` as an incomplete refresh; `success: true` only means the refresh command ran. A malformed model configuration returns a failed response.
+
+```json
+{"type": "response", "command": "refresh_models", "success": true, "data": {"models": [], "aborted": false, "errors": {}}}
+```
+
 ## Thinking
 
 ### set_thinking_level
@@ -416,6 +430,18 @@ Response:
 {"type": "response", "command": "set_auto_compaction", "success": true}
 ```
 
+### set_compaction_reserve_tokens
+
+Set a non-negative safe integer reserve for the live session. `null` clears the runtime override and restores the configured value for the current model. The override applies to manual and automatic compaction without reloading extensions or changing queued messages. It is not saved to `settings.json` or carried into another session.
+
+```json
+{"type": "set_compaction_reserve_tokens", "reserveTokens": 32000}
+```
+
+```json
+{"type": "response", "command": "set_compaction_reserve_tokens", "success": true, "data": {"reserveTokens": 32000}}
+```
+
 ## Retry
 
 ### set_auto_retry
